# Reference template updates

After editing `tester-v1/configs/reference/` (unless the user says not to sync):

## Live models

All subdirs of `tester-v1/configs/` except `reference/`. Discover dynamically; do not hardcode slugs.

Each live dir should have `model.yaml` and usually `bench/` (model-local, not synced from reference). Optional extra variant dirs are model-specific.

## Do not

1. Copy `reference/{variant}/` into live models. Calibration reads reference via `--server` / `--client`.
2. Create or update `calibration-footprint/`, `calibration-ctx-probe/`, or `hello-world-baseline/` under live models.
3. Delete live variant dirs that are absent from `reference/` (e.g. `bench/`).
4. Overwrite live `model.yaml` from `reference/model.yaml` (reference `model.yaml` is a structural template only).

If a slug lacks `model.yaml`, ask the user for `gguf_path` before writing.

## Notify the user

Report: which `reference/` files changed; live dirs were not given probe copies; any missing `model.yaml`; model-specific dirs left untouched.
